      ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If we let $u=2x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
